  "sourceFindings": [
    "server.build_replica_until records parallel_snapshot_wait around reader capacity reservation or capacity wait outside authority.",
    "ReaderAdmission.reserve_until checks capacity, queues FIFO admission and reserves before authority capture; its single-use reservation carries no historical root.",
    "Prepared transaction retains snapshot registration/private blob bytes after replica facade drops, including its later authority commit wait.",
    "Generated MAX_PINNED_ENTITY_SNAPSHOTS=64, WRITER_PIN_RESERVE=8; available reader handle capacity56. Persistent/root-pin and GC safety must not be weakened.",
    "Resource probe reports63 logical CPUs, roughly220GB memory headroom and512 maximum connections in application diagnostic. This does not itself justify increasing pin limits."
  ],
  "interpretation": [
    "Both profiled windows correct and healthy, no history compactions, original1000ms scheduled-stream gate still fails.",
    "Application sampled slow event requests show roughly143-268ms snapshot wait and45-103ms FIFO wait, with sub/millisecond-scale store/commit work. Embedded samples also show substantial snapshot and FIFO wait plus pre-dispatch queue time.",
    "These are sampled wall-clock spans, not CPU measurements, and client percentile edges are logarithmic upper buckets. Nested stages and cross-request totals must not be added.",
    "One diagnostic window per transport is not a robust unprofiled performance or all-scenario SQLite verdict.",
    "Client/socket profiling coverage differs for embedded; operation counts/stage scopes must be checked before comparison."
  ],
  "next": "Inspect reader capacity reservation and prepared snapshot pin lifecycle; measure queue occupancy/saturation and preserve GC exclusion, cancellation/deadlines, poison and exact commit fencing before proposing a runtime optimization."
